   "notes": [
    "pod-level cgroup: these container_* series have no `container` label, so each covers every container in the pod together, not one container. For a single-container pod that is the container's figure plus a little overhead.",
    "container_oom_events_total at pod level does NOT count kills of the containers inside the pod: it reads 0 through any number of container OOM kills. A zero here is not evidence against OOM; use the termination reason series (kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason) instead.",
    "scraped kubernetes-nodes-cadvisor every 15s: a container life or a spike shorter than the interval may fall between two samples and not appear at all; a peak is the highest value sampled, not necessarily the highest reached.",
    "a peak at 98% or more of the limit means usage reached the limit in a sampled moment; between samples it may have gone higher only to be killed, which no sample shows",
    "lives: each life from its start to its recorded termination, with the working set sampled inside it. A life with fewer than two samples shows no shape. One whose first sample is near the limit did not climb within the life; rising_reached_limit_within says how long the others took from their start"
   ],
