   "job": "kube-state-metrics",
   "notes": [
    "kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason holds the reason of the most recent termination, one sample per scrape. Counting its samples measures how long each reason was the latest one, not how many kills had it; restarts closer together than the scrape interval are not all seen.",
    "kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total is a count since the pod started. A range shows restarts back to the oldest retained sample, not the pod's whole life; a value already above zero at the first sample means restarts began before it.",
    "scraped kube-state-metrics every 15s: a container life or a spike shorter than the interval may fall between two samples and not appear at all; a peak is the highest value sampled, not necessarily the highest reached.",
    "restart_count_at_first_sample above zero: the container was already restarting when the first retained sample was taken, so the onset is before the window and is not observed (onset_in_window false)"
   ],
